Description:
To carry out an external board effectiveness review of Historic England's board (known as the Commission) during 2026.

      To carry out a BER with the completed report available by mid-November 2026 and then present and discuss that report with Commission in person on 10 December 2026.  The successful consultancy will devise its own approach but at a minimum they will include:
      •	a meeting with the Head of Governance (in person or online) before commencing work;
      •	observation at one or more meetings of Commission in person (meetings are held in London) (approximately three hours);
      •	interviews of Commissioners including the Chairman, whether in person or online;
      •	interviews (in person or online) of several senior staff including the Co-CEOs;
      •	a written survey of all Commissioners;
      •	and scrutiny of documents relating to Commission and its work such as terms of reference, minutes etcetera.

Additional Text:
Organisations who would like to attend the Market Engagement Event on  Monday 13th April at 2pm should contact  wlm-tr.nwlcamhspc@nhs.net advising of the names of staff who will be attending the event.

DISCLAIMERS: 

West London NHS Trust is still finalising its decision in regard to future service provision and is inviting market engagement to seek the views and opinions of those organisations that may be interested to become involved to delivering this future service; 

This Market Engagement Event (MEE) , and any subsequent information provided in response to it, does not form an integral part of any potential future procurement exercise and should be considered as an attempt by the Trust to engage with the potential market for delivering the  services;

This MEE, the accompanying information and the responses received arising from it are in no way legally binding on any party; 

Participation in the engagement exercise is not a mandatory requirement for participating in any potential future procurement; however, responses received will assist to inform West London NHS Trust as to the level of interest from the market 

Any responses and information that are shared through this market engagement exercise may be used by West London NHS Trust to inform development of the final service specification prior to a formal tender process.

Description:
Partnership Fund for a Resilient Ukraine Phase 2 (PFRU-2) is a multi-year, multi-donor-funded programme managed by the UK's Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office.
As part of its project activities, PFRU-2 is seeking an organization to supply the Modular Boiler House.

Please note the following important tender provisions:
•	the deadline for submitting proposals is March 20, 2026, at 15:00 Kyiv time; extended till 10 April, 2026, at 15:00 Kyiv time;
•	all questions regarding the tender conditions must be submitted no later than March 13, 2026, at 18:00 Kyiv time;
•	Price proposals must be submitted either in Ukrainian or English;
•	All tender-related communication must be conducted exclusively in writing via email at pfruprocurement@chemonics.com;
•	The PFRU-2 project is exempt from taxes, fees, and VAT in the partner country. Therefore, PFRU-2 will make payments for services excluding VAT;
•	Email for submitting proposals: pfruprocurement@chemonics.com;
•	When sending proposals or inquiries via email, it is mandatory to include the tender number PFRU2-2025-412 in the email subject line.

Proposal Submission Instructions:

ITT_PFRU2-2025-412 - review the tender conditions;
Volume 3_Terms of Reference - complete the document, sign the original scan/convert to PDF and sign electronically and submit the completed Excel file and the signed document as part of the proposal.
Annex 1 - complete either the English or Ukrainian version and sign the original or scan/convert to PDF and sign electronically and include it in the proposal submission.

Registration documents that follow the laws of your country must be part of the proposal.

The Services required by the MHRA shall include monitoring (covering UK, regional and international media sources/outlets):

a)	Print media - the monitoring of specified search keywords within national, regional, international and specialist / trade press and magazines;
b)	Digital/Online media - the monitoring of news and specialist / trade websites' content that includes the specified search keywords - including monitoring of non-written content, such as infographics and imagery;
c)	Broadcast - the monitoring of content on television, radio and web broadcasts and podcasts that includes the specified search keywords;
d)	Human-driven Media Evaluation and Analysis - the selection, evaluation and analysis of the monitored media items through human review, to be reported on a quarterly basis;
e)	Automated Media Evaluation and Analysis - the automated assessment and analysis of the monitored media items;
f)	A Journalists/Media Contact Database - a database listing media contacts, contact details, biographies and sector of interest etc.

The Supplier shall deliver the monitoring results and alerts in accordance with the agreed monitoring brief (keywords, themes etc) and timelines, customised as agreed for the relevant Buyer's representatives/users. The service is required 24/7 all year. 

This procurement is being concluded following a competition under the CCS DPS RM6126 Research & Insights.
